  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chikanta Community Schools Cooking Oil Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Chikanta Community Schools (CCS) has 50 community school-based womens groups that it facilitates with income generating activities. Each community womens group has an average of 15 members that grow various crops ranging from vegetables, maize and oilseed crops which they have challenges marketing. The CCS wishes to establish a processing and marketing enterprise that will purchase oilseeds (groundnuts and sunflower) from members and the community and process it into cooking oil for sell to the community and surrounding locations</narrative>
  </description>
